==================== Input ====================
# `sortOpenapi.keyOrder` replaces one table and leaves every other one intact.
#
# Here `get` is overridden to `[summary, operationId]`, which is not its built-in order (that starts
# with `operationId`). So:
#
# `get`     -> the override: `summary` first, then `operationId`, then the unlisted keys
#              (`responses`, `tags`) case-insensitively.
# `post`    -> untouched. Its built-in table still applies, `operationId` first. This is the layering:
#              upstream's `--sortFile` replaces the whole set, so naming only `get` there would
#              silently disable `post`, `requestBody` and `responses` as well.
# `requestBody` and `responses` -> also untouched, for the same reason.
openapi: 3.0.0
paths:
  /p:
    get:
      responses: {}
      tags: [t]
      operationId: op
      summary: s
    post:
      responses: {}
      summary: s
      operationId: op
      requestBody:
        content: {}
        required: true
        description: d

==================== Output ====================
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ printWidth: 80, sortOpenapi: {"keyOrder":{"get":["summary","operationId"]}} }
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `sortOpenapi.keyOrder` replaces one table and leaves every other one intact.
#
# Here `get` is overridden to `[summary, operationId]`, which is not its built-in order (that starts
# with `operationId`). So:
#
# `get`     -> the override: `summary` first, then `operationId`, then the unlisted keys
#              (`responses`, `tags`) case-insensitively.
# `post`    -> untouched. Its built-in table still applies, `operationId` first. This is the layering:
#              upstream's `--sortFile` replaces the whole set, so naming only `get` there would
#              silently disable `post`, `requestBody` and `responses` as well.
# `requestBody` and `responses` -> also untouched, for the same reason.
openapi: 3.0.0
paths:
  /p:
    get:
      summary: s
      operationId: op
      responses: {}
      tags: [t]
    post:
      operationId: op
      summary: s
      requestBody:
        description: d
        required: true
        content: {}
      responses: {}

